  "coverage_note": "This is the final additive affected-surface campaign. The original 1204-file/10635-test full renderer and 179-file/1618-test full TUI aggregates remain in fe13-validation.json against their original source. Overlapping focused counts are not added to those aggregates. No second native/platform aggregate, packaging attempt or browser navigation was made.",
  "implementation": [
    "Existing overview mounts exact operator inspection/audit/retention/checkpoint and separately confirmed broker repair/deletion plans. Logical deletion remains partial; no personal-harness or complete-erasure claim.",
    "Account-pinned Gmail-thread/calendar selection performs explicit prepare, reads every cached preview chunk, checks full size/SHA and exact proposal/approval identities, renders inert complete text, and requires independent original/projection review before separate publication. No refetch during publication or unpinned fallback.",
    "Named configured specialist catalog, responsibility/grants/isolated memory, typed immutable references/constraints, exact preview and separately confirmed single-child handoff; stable command status and parent review remain explicit. Teams remain disabled.",
    "Strict speech explicit finite admission precedes recording/synthesis; stable request/account IDs and inline budget usage are separate from mission acceptance. Client microphone/playback remain explicit and scoped. Lost final speech usage retains the original identity even after discard; inspect-only, no audio replay or budget reset.",
    "Explicit selected-project bounded deterministic opportunity discovery/list/history and exact CAS save/dismiss/accept; accepted choice navigates to existing review control with scoped target context and creates no work or approval.",
    "Same-object reconnect/generation and scope changes invalidate pending review. Passive recovery cache distinguishes operator/speech/specialist/opportunity IDs, never restores approval, and has bounded lifetime/capacity. Nine-locale copy uses existing i18n authority."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "Worker and initial parent desktop type probes hit default 2 GiB heap OOM (exit134); original logs retained.",
    "First clean desktop typecheck with 4 GiB heap ran concurrently with renderer build/lint and was killed (exit137). Retried once serially after those completed with the same heap; final result is listed separately.",
    "Initial clean web build compiled but its build-input fingerprint guard caught whitespace-only normalization in connected-source test during compilation. Stable-tree retry is recorded separately; no semantic code change.",
    "One new integration test initially had incomplete synthetic i18n notification copy; fixed fixture and affected wiring rerun passed14 tests before clean runtime aggregate.",
    "Untracked source-test trailing spaces normalized; final source hashes below include that metadata-only change."
  ],
